# Screens: the wrist panel. Y (the left controller's upper button) opens the quick actions on a panel over the left wrist
# and Y again closes it; the right hand's laser and trigger press its tiles: Dampeners switches the dampeners, Inventory,
# Terminal and the G menu open their screens, which stand in the world ahead of the eyes, and B goes back out of them.
# The panel follows the left hand: with the hand where this file holds it, the panel's middle is 0.3 m from the right
# hand placed and turned as below, square on, and 0.3 m wide (1920 GUI pixels); each tile's place on it is the plugin's
# grid of 3 by 4 tiles (QuickActionsScreen.Layout).

plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet

# ---- What the world needs: the astronaut on foot in gravity (Earth Planet starts so). Nothing is built. ---------------

# Dampeners on, so the Dampeners tile has something to switch off.
dampeners on
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

# ---- Y opens and closes the panel -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Headset level, the left hand held out low before the body, the right hand resting below, aimed down.
head 0 1.6 0
hand left -0.2 1.1 -0.35
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 1
# Before: only the game is up.
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
# Index's left B is the Y button.
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
expect log Wrist panel: opened (Y), 12 tiles within 5
expect log Menu opened on the wrist within 5
# Y again closes it.
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
expect log Wrist panel: closed (Y) within 5

# ---- Where the panel is drawn: on the left wrist, near, low and to the left, and it stays with the hand ----------------

# Looking down at the left hand, as a player does to use the panel. With the hand where this file holds it, the panel's
# middle is about 0.5 m ahead of the eyes, 18 degrees left of the middle of the view and 10 below it, and it is 0.3 m
# wide, about 35 degrees (Rendering/WorldMenu.cs, WristPose).
head 0 1.6 0 0 -45
wait 1
expect headset steady
headset wrist-closed.png
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
headset wrist-open.png
expect headset new depth 0.25 0.8
expect headset new at -18 -10 15
expect headset new size 20 50
# Looking further down, the panel stays on the wrist: the view moves past it, as it does past the world.
head 0 1.6 0 0 -60
wait 1
headset wrist-look-down.png
expect headset new follows world
# Y closes it, and the head is level again for the rest of the test.
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
head 0 1.6 0
wait 1
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

# ---- The laser presses a tile: Dampeners ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

read character
expect dampeners == true
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
# The right hand's laser on the Dampeners tile, and its trigger.
hand right -0.128 1.438 -0.013 -36.5 -56.1
wait 1
expect log '/Laser: pointing at the panel, GUI [(]3[0-9][0-9], 6[0-9][0-9][)]/' within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
wait 1.5
# The game's own Dampeners control was pressed and the panel closed.
expect log '/Wrist panel: .Dampeners. read by the game/' within 5
read character
expect dampeners == false
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

# ---- The tiles that open screens: Inventory, Terminal, G menu, each in the world ahead -------------------------------

hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
# The right hand's laser on the Inventory tile, and its trigger.
hand right -0.158 1.473 -0.054 -36.5 -56.1
wait 1
expect log '/Laser: pointing at the panel, GUI [(]3[0-9][0-9], 2[0-9][0-9][)]/' within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
wait 1.5
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal
expect log Menu opened; panel placed within 5
# B goes back: the screen closes and the game has the focus again.
press right b
wait 0.2
release right b
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
# The right hand's laser on the Terminal tile, and its trigger.
hand right -0.082 1.473 -0.111 -36.5 -56.1
wait 1
expect log '/Laser: pointing at the panel, GUI [(]9[0-9][0-9], 2[0-9][0-9][)]/' within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
wait 1.5
read screens
expect result contains MyGuiScreenTerminal
press right b
wait 0.2
release right b
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay

# G menu: some screen other than the game and the panel has the focus.
hand right 0.25 1.0 -0.3 0 -60
wait 0.5
press left b
wait 0.2
release left b
wait 1
read screen
expect type == QuickActionsScreen
# The right hand's laser on the G menu tile, and its trigger.
hand right -0.006 1.473 -0.167 -36.5 -56.1
wait 1
expect log '/Laser: pointing at the panel, GUI [(]1[45][0-9][0-9], 2[0-9][0-9][)]/' within 5
press right trigger
wait 0.2
release right trigger
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type != MyGuiScreenGamePlay
expect type != QuickActionsScreen
press right b
wait 0.2
release right b
wait 1.5
read screen
expect type == MyGuiScreenGamePlay
# The datapad is left out of this release: nothing of it ran.
expect no log Datapad
expect no log Exception
